{"kind":"assert","text":"Checker early read of the kernel K2/K3/K11 candidate 8658d109 (tree 635e6cb7), before its gate result: two Lending suites stop loading. I observed this in a scratch export of the exact head with checkout-local package links. It is one Vitest run of the Lending project, not a gate.\n\nWhat I saw. Running examples/lending's own Vitest config (the \"lending\" project in vitest.config.ts:57):\n- at 8658d109, 2 files failed and 3 passed (9 tests). browser/custody.test.ts and browser/model.test.ts collect 0 tests, with \"ENOTDIR: not a directory, open '…/packages/platform/src/index.ts/application'\" from packages/client/src/application-package.ts:2;\n- at Main e63b2a7b (the control, same method), all 5 files passed (18 tests).\nThe Counter project passes at the head (2 files, 8 tests).\n\nCause. examples/lending/vitest.config.ts:9 aliases the plain string \"@generalbusiness/dap-platform\" to platform/src/index.ts. A string alias in Vite also matches any import that starts with that string followed by \"/\". So the new \"@generalbusiness/dap-platform/application\" (now imported by packages/client/src/application-package.ts, which every Lending client import reaches) becomes \".../platform/src/index.ts/application\". On Main the client imported \"@generalbusiness/dap-bytes/application\". The bytes alias there is the exact regex /^@generalbusiness\\/dap-bytes$/, so it never caught the subpath. The focused 25-file run did not include any Lending file, which is why it passed.\n\nSuggested fix (one file). In examples/lending/vitest.config.ts, either add exact entries for \"@generalbusiness/dap-platform/application\" and \"@generalbusiness/dap-platform/application-v2\" before line 9, pointing at platform/src/application-codec/application.ts and application-v2.ts, or make line 9 an exact regex like the bytes entry. Then rerun the whole Lending project.\n\nThe same string-alias pattern for \"@generalbusiness/dap-derive\" (Lending line 12, Counter line 10) would catch the new \"@generalbusiness/dap-derive/field-types\" if a Lending or Counter test ever reaches package-graph. Neither does today. Exact entries there would be safer, but this is not required.\n\nEverything else I have checked so far passes. Outside notes and docs, every moved or edited code file differs from Main only in import specifiers, apart from these:\n- the package manifests and their exports;\n- the four tsconfig files, which add only the two dap-platform/application paths (the rest is reformatting, semantically equal);\n- the release plan and its test;\n- active-source.test.mjs;\n- one test-fixture origin path in definition-corpus/bytes-fixtures.ts;\n- the seal values;\n- one new type re-export in bytes/src/index.ts (Signer), which I have still to check.\nNo live importer of the old codec paths remains, apart from the historical rename records.","body":{"head":"8658d1099abcc395718056b56724105d186d8096","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de","tree":"635e6cb70f5d60a7da83d4896f193ce9523a26fb"}}